  <section>
    <div class="wide">
      {{> components/pattern-examples topic="send-results"}}
      <p>Looking at a bounce received after SMTP accepted your message? Use <a href="/delivery-reports.html">Reading delivery reports</a>.
        This page describes submission facts; the notification Email describes what a delivery system reported later.</p>
      <p>
        A send can throw even though the SMTP server accepted the message for some recipients. Retrying the original email could then send those
        recipients another copy. A <code>MailSubmissionReceipt</code> tells you what is known about that attempt, including individual recipient
        replies and which recipients, if any, are candidates for a retry.
      </p>
      <p>
        SMTP conversations and output are illustrative, not replies you should expect from a particular server.
        Acceptance here always means SMTP submission, not final mailbox delivery or inbox placement.
      </p>
      <p>For a visual map of the pieces producing these results and observer callbacks, see
        <a href="/sending-and-execution.html#section-send-architecture">Inside a mail send</a>.</p>
      <p>To join actual sends to application traces and aggregated metrics, use the optional
        <a href="/opentelemetry.html">OpenTelemetry integration</a>. It records terminal completion directly,
        independently of progress coalescing or result-observer dispatch.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

